# Local agent tooling. Everything under .claude/ is per-machine assistant setup
# -- settings, hooks, worktrees, generated state -- and is not shared, with ONE
# exception: .claude/sassy-dog/, the config the optional sassy-dog Claude Code
# plugin (the public Sassy-Dog/skills) reads when someone invokes one of its
# skills. It is tracked so every worktree, machine and reviewer sees the same
# config. A contributor who never installs the plugin is unaffected: nothing
# else reads it. It is not inert, though: `preflight_commands` runs as a shell
# command, and tidy-repo.md's lists decide what an untracked-file sweep
# deletes, so review changes there like changes to scripts/.
#
# Everything else stays out, deliberately. A committed settings.json buys
# nothing (a cloud session never loads a repository's `enabledPlugins`), and
# its hooks would run with no trust prompt in parent-trusted, `claude -p`/SDK
# and cloud sessions; committed hooks/ scripts would also become editable by
# any PR. (#259 removed an earlier `!.claude/hooks/` carve-out for leaking
# filenames and provenance markers while the plugin was private.)
#
# Never commit a per-checkout key there, `execution_site` above all: it names
# the one machine a checkout answers to, and a committed one would claim every
# clone is that machine.
#
# Excluding `.claude/*`, not `.claude/`, is what makes the re-include possible:
# git cannot re-include a path under an excluded directory, so `.claude/` +
# `!...` re-includes nothing. The last two lines then narrow sassy-dog/ to
# exactly what the plugin reads, `<name>.md` one level deep. An ignore rule is
# only a default (`git add -f` tracks an ignored path anyway), so
# scripts/claude-dir-guard.sh fails CI if anything else named .claude is ever
# tracked.
.claude/*
!.claude/sassy-dog/
.claude/sassy-dog/*
!.claude/sassy-dog/*.md
# Serena MCP's per-project state (cache, memories, project.yml): per-machine,
# self-created the moment the server touches the repo. Deny-by-default with no
# carve-outs.
.serena/

# direnv: `.envrc` is committed and holds no values; the real ones live here.
.envrc.local
.direnv/

# Assistant tooling output. Kept on the machine that produced it, not shared.
docs/superpowers/

# A minisign private key regenerated for the agent feed fixtures
# (tests/fixtures/README.md) must never be committed; only its public half is.
tests/fixtures/**/*.key

# Throwaway artifacts (screenshots, scratch scripts, review copies) — never committed.
tmp/

# Codex local hook config (per-machine tooling, not shared).
.codex/
